# haproxy-topology.drawio

Import the following Mermaid layout into draw.io:

```mermaid
graph TD
    CLIENTS[Client Systems]

    subgraph LOADBALANCER[HAProxy Load Balancer]
        LB01[LB01\n192.168.100.30]
    end

    subgraph WEBPOOL[Backend Web Servers]
        WEB01[WEB01\n192.168.100.20]
        WEB02[WEB02\n192.168.100.21]
    end

    CLIENTS --> LB01
    LB01 --> WEB01
    LB01 --> WEB02
```

Recommended draw.io styling:

- Use dark theme
- Use orange for HAProxy node
- Use blue for web servers
- Use green for clients
- Add arrows for traffic flow
- Add title:
  HAProxy Load Balancer Topology

Validation notes:

- HAProxy frontend listens on port 80
- Backend servers use Apache HTTP Server
- Load balancing method:
  roundrobin

Suggested export filename:

```text
haproxy-topology.png
